## CRITICAL PROJECT CONSTRAINTS

### 1. NEVER Break Multi-Tenant Isolation
```php
// ❌ ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN - Never add tenant_id columns
Schema::table('orders', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->foreignId('tenant_id'); // ❌ NEVER!
});

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Never query across tenants
$allOrders = DB::connection('mysql')->table('orders')->get(); // ❌ NEVER!

// ✅ ALWAYS - Trust database switching
tenancy()->initialize($tenant);
$orders = Order::all(); // Automatically scoped to tenant DB

// ✅ ALWAYS - Test tenant isolation for every new feature
public function test_tenant_isolation_for_new_feature(): void
{
    // Create data in tenant 1
    // Switch to tenant 2
    // Verify tenant 2 cannot access tenant 1 data
}
```

### 2. PRESERVE Business Logic from Old System
```php
// The old system (Laravel 5.8) had rich business logic.
// When migrating features, ALWAYS check old_version_source/ for:
// - Calculation formulas
// - Validation rules
// - Workflow automation
// - Event handling

// Example: Order montage time calculation
// ✅ CORRECT - Replicate old logic exactly
protected function montageTime(): Attribute
{
    // Formula from old_version_source/app/Order.php:636
    return Attribute::make(
        get: fn () => $this->articles->reduce(function($carry, $art) {
            return $carry + $art->pivot->quantity * $art->pivot->montage_time;
        }, 0),
    );
}

// ❌ WRONG - Don't guess or simplify calculations
protected function montageTime(): Attribute
{
    return Attribute::make(
        get: fn () => $this->articles->count() * 8, // ❌ Oversimplified!
    );
}
```

