## DATABASE MIGRATION RULES

### Migration Location Rules
```php
// ✅ Tenant tables go in database/migrations/tenant/
// These tables are created in EACH tenant database
database/migrations/tenant/
    - create_orders_table.php
    - create_clients_table.php
    - create_documents_table.php

// ✅ Central tables go in database/migrations/
// These tables exist ONLY in the central database
database/migrations/
    - create_tenants_table.php
    - create_domains_table.php
    - create_super_admins_table.php

// ❌ NEVER put tenant tables in central migrations
// ❌ NEVER put central tables in tenant migrations
```

### Migration Best Practices
```php
// ✅ ALWAYS add indexes for foreign keys
Schema::create('orders', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('client_id')->constrained()->onDelete('cascade');
    // constrained() automatically adds index
});

// ✅ ALWAYS make nullable what should be nullable
$table->date('install_date')->nullable(); // Not always known at creation
$table->decimal('price_to_customer', 10, 2)->nullable(); // May not be set yet

// ✅ ALWAYS use meaningful default values
$table->boolean('is_confirmed')->default(false);
$table->string('status')->default('pending');

// ✅ NEVER delete migrations that ran in production
// Instead, create a new migration to modify the table

// ✅ ALWAYS provide down() method
public function down(): void
{
    Schema::dropIfExists('orders');
}
```

