## API DEVELOPMENT RULES

### API Route Organization
```php
// routes/api.php - Public endpoints (central database)
Route::post('/login', [AuthController::class, 'login']);
Route::post('/register', [AuthController::class, 'register']);

// routes/api.php - Authenticated + Tenant-aware (via X-Tenant-ID header)
Route::middleware(['auth:sanctum', 'tenant.header'])->group(function () {
    Route::get('/orders', [OrderController::class, 'index']);
    Route::post('/orders', [OrderController::class, 'store']);
});

// ✅ ALWAYS return API resources
public function index(Request $request): JsonResponse
{
    $orders = Order::with(['client', 'place'])
        ->paginate($request->get('per_page', 15));
    
    return OrderResource::collection($orders)
        ->response()
        ->setStatusCode(200);
}

// ✅ ALWAYS validate with Form Requests
public function store(StoreOrderRequest $request): JsonResponse
{
    $order = Order::create($request->validated());
    
    return (new OrderResource($order))
        ->response()
        ->setStatusCode(201);
}
```

