## SECURITY CHECKLIST

### Before Committing Any Code
```
✅ Input validated (Form Request or manual validation)
✅ Authorization checked (Policy or permission)
✅ SQL injection prevented (use Eloquent or parameter binding)
✅ XSS prevented (Blade {{ }} auto-escapes, use {!! !!} only when needed)
✅ CSRF token included (forms, AJAX)
✅ Mass assignment protected ($fillable defined)
✅ Tenant isolation maintained (test written)
✅ File uploads validated (size, type, malware scan if needed)
✅ Sensitive data not logged
✅ API rate limiting applied
```

### Permission Naming Convention
```php
// Format: {resource}.{action}
Permission::create(['name' => 'orders.view']);
Permission::create(['name' => 'orders.create']);
Permission::create(['name' => 'orders.edit']);
Permission::create(['name' => 'orders.delete']);
Permission::create(['name' => 'orders.finish']); // Special action

// Use in code
if (auth()->user()->hasPermissionTo('orders.finish')) {
    $order->update(['is_finished' => true]);
}

// Use in Filament resource
public static function canEdit(Model $record): bool
{
    return auth()->user()->can('update', $record);
}
