## PERFORMANCE GUIDELINES

### Database Query Optimization
```php
// ✅ ALWAYS eager load relationships
$orders = Order::with([
    'client.company',
    'place',
    'articles',
    'user'
])->get();

// ✅ Use select() to limit columns
$orders = Order::select(['id', 'number', 'client_id'])
    ->with('client:id,name')
    ->get();

// ✅ Use chunk() for large datasets
Order::chunk(100, function ($orders) {
    foreach ($orders as $order) {
        // Process order
    }
});

// ❌ NEVER do this (N+1 problem)
$orders = Order::all();
foreach ($orders as $order) {
    echo $order->client->name; // N queries!
}
```

### Caching Strategy
```php
// ✅ Cache expensive queries (tenant-scoped)
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Cache;

public function getOrderStatistics(): array
{
    return Cache::remember(
        "tenant.{$this->id}.order_stats",
        now()->addMinutes(15),
        fn () => [
            'total' => Order::count(),
            'pending' => Order::where('is_finished', false)->count(),
            'revenue' => Order::sum('price_to_customer'),
        ]
    );
}

// ✅ Invalidate cache on changes
protected function invalidateOrderStatsCache(): void
{
    Cache::forget("tenant.{tenant('id')}.order_stats");
}

// Use in observer
class OrderObserver
{
    public function created(Order $order): void
    {
        $this->invalidateOrderStatsCache();
    }
}
```

### Queue Long-Running Tasks
```php
// ✅ Queue tasks that take > 3 seconds
use App\Jobs\GenerateOrderReport;

public function generateReport(Order $order): void
{
    GenerateOrderReport::dispatch($order)
        ->onQueue('reports');
}

// Job class
class GenerateOrderReport implements ShouldQueue
{
    use Queueable, SerializesModels;
    
    public function __construct(
        public Order $order
    ) {}
    
    public function handle(): void
    {
        // Ensure tenant context
        tenancy()->initialize(tenant());
        
        // Generate report...
    }
}
```

